(Advanced Database Systems - Lecture Notes) Tj T*
(Unit 3: Normalization) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Normalization is the process of organizing the attributes and relations of a relational) Tj T*
(database to reduce data redundancy and improve data integrity. A poorly designed relation) Tj T*
(suffers from update anomalies: an insertion anomaly occurs when we cannot record a fact) Tj T*
(without also recording an unrelated fact, a deletion anomaly occurs when deleting one fact) Tj T*
(unintentionally removes another, and a modification anomaly occurs when the same fact is) Tj T*
(stored in many rows and must be updated everywhere.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Normalization works by decomposing relations into smaller relations based on functional) Tj T*
(dependencies. A functional dependency X -> Y holds when each value of X determines exactly) Tj T*
(one value of Y. The normal forms 1NF, 2NF, 3NF and BCNF are progressively stricter) Tj T*
(conditions on these dependencies.) Tj T*
ET
