(First Normal Form \(1NF\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A relation is in first normal form when every attribute contains only atomic \(indivisible\)) Tj T*
(values and there are no repeating groups. Each row must be identifiable by a primary key.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Example: a table STUDENT\(StudentID, Name, Courses\) where Courses holds the list "DBMS,) Tj T*
(Networks, AI" violates 1NF because the Courses attribute is multi-valued. To convert it to) Tj T*
(1NF we create one row per student and course: ENROLLMENT\(StudentID, Name, Course\) with rows) Tj T*
(\(101, Asha, DBMS\), \(101, Asha, Networks\) and \(101, Asha, AI\). Now every attribute value is) Tj T*
(atomic.) Tj T*
ET
