(Second Normal Form \(2NF\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A relation is in second normal form when it is in 1NF and every non-key attribute is fully) Tj T*
(functionally dependent on the whole primary key. 2NF only matters when the primary key is) Tj T*
(composite. A partial dependency exists when a non-key attribute depends on only part of a) Tj T*
(composite key.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Example: ENROLLMENT\(StudentID, CourseID, StudentName, CourseTitle, Grade\) has the composite) Tj T*
(key \(StudentID, CourseID\). StudentName depends only on StudentID and CourseTitle depends) Tj T*
(only on CourseID, which are partial dependencies. Decompose into STUDENT\(StudentID,) Tj T*
(StudentName\), COURSE\(CourseID, CourseTitle\) and ENROLLMENT\(StudentID, CourseID, Grade\). Each) Tj T*
(relation is now in 2NF.) Tj T*
ET
