(Third Normal Form \(3NF\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A relation is in third normal form when it is in 2NF and no non-key attribute is) Tj T*
(transitively dependent on the primary key. A transitive dependency exists when a non-key) Tj T*
(attribute depends on another non-key attribute, for example A -> B and B -> C, so A -> C.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Example: EMPLOYEE\(EmpID, EmpName, DeptID, DeptName\). EmpID -> DeptID and DeptID -> DeptName,) Tj T*
(so DeptName is transitively dependent on EmpID. Decompose into EMPLOYEE\(EmpID, EmpName,) Tj T*
(DeptID\) and DEPARTMENT\(DeptID, DeptName\). Changing a department name now requires updating a) Tj T*
(single row, which removes the modification anomaly.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Boyce-Codd Normal Form \(BCNF\) is a stronger version of 3NF: for every non-trivial functional) Tj T*
(dependency X -> Y, X must be a superkey.) Tj T*
ET
