(Unit 4: Transactions and Concurrency Control) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A transaction is a logical unit of work that must satisfy the ACID properties. Atomicity) Tj T*
(means all operations of a transaction complete or none do. Consistency means a transaction) Tj T*
(moves the database from one valid state to another. Isolation means concurrent transactions) Tj T*
(do not interfere with each other. Durability means committed changes survive system) Tj T*
(failures, typically by writing to a write-ahead log.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Concurrency control prevents problems such as lost updates, dirty reads and unrepeatable) Tj T*
(reads. Two-phase locking \(2PL\) guarantees conflict serializability: in the growing phase a) Tj T*
(transaction acquires locks and releases none, and in the shrinking phase it releases locks) Tj T*
(and acquires none. Strict 2PL holds all exclusive locks until commit, which also prevents) Tj T*
(cascading aborts.) Tj T*
ET
